  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Monday)\nIssued at 151 AM CDT Tue Oct 20 2026\n\nThe upper ridge will gradually shift east late this week into the \nweekend as the upper trough continues to slowly approach and \neventually move across the Plains. Models diverge on the \ntiming/evolution of this trough over the weekend into next week. \nHowever, right now it looks like the trough will bring a chance for \nsome more rain and maybe some storms over the weekend into early \nnext week. Currently, rainfall totals do not look as high (3+ \ninches) as what occurred in some areas with the last couple of rain \nevents but some locations, primarily in western parts of the fa, \nmight see as much as an 1 to 1.5 inches. The uncertainties of the \ntiming/evolution of this system will have an impact on when/where \nrain chances will occur which could also have an impact on amounts \nso will have to wait and see how things come together.\n\nTemperatures are expected to remain near or above average for late \nOctober over the weekend into early next week although with maybe a \nslight cool down early next week.",
